# Line endings, and why this file has to exist.
#
# The failure messages are this tool's product and they are held byte-for-byte
# by goldens in testdata/. On a Windows checkout with the default core.autocrlf,
# git rewrites those goldens to CRLF on the way out, the tool still renders LF,
# and fourteen golden tests fail with "that is a contract change, not a diff to
# regenerate" about a contract nobody touched. The tests are right and the
# checkout is wrong.
* text=auto eol=lf

# testdata/ is exempt from translation in both directions, not merely pinned to
# LF. One golden is deliberately CRLF: line-endings-under-strict.txt is the
# fixture for the diagnostic that tells an agent its payload is LF and the file
# is not. Normalising it would delete the thing it tests.
#
# -text is stronger than eol=lf here on purpose. It says these bytes are never
# git's business, which is exactly the claim a golden makes.
testdata/** -text

# Shipped as executable and run by git itself. Nothing should rewrite them.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
